# Personal defaults — applies to every project on this machine

> Copy this to `~/.claude/CLAUDE.md` before the workshop so the hierarchy demo
> has three layers (global → project → subdirectory).

## How I like Claude to work with me

- Be terse. Don't summarize what you just did at the end of every response — the diff already shows it.
- For exploratory questions, give me 2-3 sentences with a recommendation, not a wall of text.
- Don't add comments that just restate what the code does.
- When you make a non-obvious choice, explain *why* — not what.

## Tool preferences I always use

- Package manager: `uv` for Python, `pnpm` for Node when available.
- Editor: VS Code. The CLI is the source of truth, the editor is for reading.
- Always prefer `rg` over `grep` when both are available.

## Things I never want

- Don't generate license headers in source files unless I ask.
- Don't add `// TODO:` comments — file an issue or fix it.
- Don't open browser windows or external apps without asking.
